        "department": "CSE",
        "description": "Randomisation and probability plays a huge role in today's algorithms, especially in two situations: the data itself has errors, or is too large and complex. This course studies algorithms which, by design, may not be correct 100% of the time, or run within the stipulated resource always, but definitely do so in an overwhelmingly large number of cases. The course will be split into three main logical sections - tools from probability theory, algorithms which are probabilistic and analysis of deterministic algorithms for different input distributions.",
